orm $z=5x+y,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275243 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5fd5b90f-0ac6-584e-ad1f-769d139ad924" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275243 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we factor the right-hand side of the given equation, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2(5x+y)}{(5x+y)+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=5x+y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=5+\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-5 & =\\frac{2z}{z+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{7z+5}{z+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=\\frac{7z+5}{z+1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487578 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{2}{x-y}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487578 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487578 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "066638b5-b947-5188-95a4-7fb8fa301ba9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487663 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{(2x-y)^{2}-1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487663 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487663 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "32b7eb7e-d784-51cc-a6f7-a2687a072eb0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487680 #edb/ref 1080 "2x+2y" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487680 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487680 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3af72acc-2cce-56f5-a188-7b04a5c4baf2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487695 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{(2x-y)^{2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487695 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487